<main>
  <h1>Hi, I'm Rameen.</h1>
  <p class="big">I'm an Information Technology student at the University of Balochistan, and I'm learning to build <span class="hl">websites</span>. I'm in my 6th semester, in the third year of a 2023&ndash;2027 degree.</p>
  <p>Most of what's on this page is me practising front-end work: HTML, CSS and a bit of JavaScript. I learn by doing, so each project below started as something I wanted to try.</p>
  <span class="note">scroll down for the projects</span>

  <section id="projects">
    <h2>Things I've made</h2>
    <p class="sub">Six so far. Click a picture to open the project.</p>

    <article class="p">
      <a class="shot" href="projects/lumora-candles/"><img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," width="1200" height="760" loading="lazy" alt="Screenshot of the Lumora Candles page"></a>
      <div>
        <h3><a href="projects/lumora-candles/">Lumora Candles</a></h3>
        <p>A product page for a soy candle brand: eight scents, burning tips and order buttons that open WhatsApp.</p>
        <p class="mono">HTML, CSS</p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="p">
      <a class="shot" href="projects/balochistan-travel-guide/"><img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," width="1200" height="760" loading="lazy" alt="Screenshot of the Balochistan Travel Guide"></a>
      <div>
        <h3><a href="projects/balochistan-travel-guide/">Balochistan Travel Guide</a></h3>
        <p>When to visit Balochistan: the best places by season, what is blooming and ripe each month, dry fruits to bring home, and travel tips.</p>
        <p class="mono">HTML, CSS</p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="p">
      <a class="shot" href="projects/glass-ui/"><img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," width="1200" height="760" loading="lazy" alt="Screenshot of the Glass UI component library"></a>
      <div>
        <h3><a href="projects/glass-ui/">Glass UI</a></h3>
        <p>A set of frosted-glass components (buttons, cards, a form and a modal) with a light and a dark theme.</p>
        <p class="mono">HTML, CSS</p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="p">
      <a class="shot" href="projects/stop-by-stop-timeline/"><img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," width="1200" height="760" loading="lazy" alt="Screenshot of the Stop by Stop timeline"></a>
      <div>
        <h3><a href="projects/stop-by-stop-timeline/">Stop by Stop</a></h3>
        <p>A timeline that scrolls like a metro line. Each stop opens to show more, and you can filter by type.</p>
        <p class="mono">HTML, CSS</p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="p">
      <a class="shot" href="projects/css-art-gallery/"><img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," width="1200" height="760" loading="lazy" alt="Screenshot of the CSS Art Gallery"></a>
      <div>
        <h3><a href="projects/css-art-gallery/">CSS Art Gallery</a></h3>
        <p>Six drawings made only with CSS (borders, shadows and pseudo-elements), with no image files. Hover over one to animate it.</p>
        <p class="mono">HTML, CSS</p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="p">
      <a class="shot" href="projects/retro-terminal/"><img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," width="1200" height="760" loading="lazy" alt="Screenshot of the Retro Terminal Portfolio"></a>
      <div>
        <h3><a href="projects/retro-terminal/">Retro Terminal Portfolio</a></h3>
        <p>A portfolio dressed up as an old green-screen computer, with a typed start-up sequence. The navigation uses only CSS.</p>
        <p class="mono">HTML, CSS</p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section id="about">
    <h2>About me</h2>
    <p>I study Information Technology at the University of Balochistan in Pakistan. My goal is to become a web developer and to fill this page with real projects, one at a time.</p>
    <dl>
      <dt>Using now</dt><dd>HTML, CSS, Bootstrap and WordPress</dd>
      <dt>Getting better at</dt><dd>JavaScript</dd>
      <dt>From university, at beginner level</dt><dd>C and C++</dd>
      <dt>Courses so far</dt><dd>Operating systems, computer organization and assembly language, computer networks, virtualization and system administration, cybersecurity, discrete structures, calculus, linear algebra, probability and statistics, and AI. For AI I gave a presentation on surface and deep learning.</dd>
      <dt>Outside of code</dt><dd>I draw, read and take photographs. Drawing goes well with my interest in how web pages look.</dd>
    </dl>
    <span class="note">yes, I draw too</span>
  </section>

  <section id="contact">
    <h2>Say hello</h2>
    <p>I'm open to learning opportunities, collaborations and web projects.</p>
    <p class="mail"><a href="mailto:rameen.hanif.it@gmail.com">rameen.hanif.it@gmail.com</a></p>
  </section>
</main>

<footer class="mono">Made by hand with HTML and CSS. Last updated October 2026.</footer>
</div>
</body>
</html>
